            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="OKE01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>O'Keeffe</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1747-06-24">
                        <placeName>Ireland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1833-02-04"/>
                    <occupation>playwright</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">See <title>DNB</title>.
   <p> Godwin has three O'Keeffe entries in the diary for 1826 when he is visiting the south 
    coast. See also letter from Adelaide O'Keeffe, his daughter, following her 
    father's death asking for Godwin's assistance with two plays her father had left her: MS. Abinger c. 14. fols. 15-16:  5 July 1833.
    The letter makes it clear that she was also present at the meetings at their home in Felpham in 1826, when Godwin was touring the south coast.</p><p> Godwin records his death. </p></note>
                    <bibl type="MS">
                        <title>MS. Abinger c. 14. fols. 15-16:  5 July 1833</title>
